WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.899
Decarbonization.

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:05.966
It's a key factor in the
fight against climate change.

00:00:05.966 --> 00:00:09.233
The goal is simple, to reduce
carbon dioxide emissions

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:11.899
around the world as soon as possible.

00:00:11.899 --> 00:00:15.933
Our planet can not be saved
unless we leave fossil fuels

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:18.000
in the ground where they belong.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.333
Decarbonization requires

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:21.899
both sweeping change
and incremental steps,

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:25.233
working industry by
industry, process by process,

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:27.400
in every major country in the world.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.699
Sound expensive?

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:30.666
It will be.

00:00:30.666 --> 00:00:32.133
But the science community agrees

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.899
that to avoid global catastrophe,

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:36.733
we have no choice but
to mobilize and take on

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:38.133
this monumental challenge.
What do we want?

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.033
Climate justice!

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.833
When do we want it?
Now!

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:42.766
Renewable energy, like wind turbines

00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:45.133
and solar panels, as
well as electric cars,

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.566
are the more popular
topics in the conversation.

00:00:47.566 --> 00:00:50.366
But there are other key sectors
that are less-discussed,

00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:52.333
and changes there are equally important

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:54.133
for decarbonizing the planet.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:55.400
Here's three.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.500
Cement, steel, and agriculture.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.000
These three sectors combined

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.033
make up almost 40% of all
carbon emissions in the world.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.933
What will it take to revolutionize

00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:08.500
these three industries
without bankrupting them?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.500
Cement is the most widley-used

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.899
manmade material in existence.

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:16.733
When combined with water and aggregates,

00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:18.366
it can be poured into whatever shape

00:01:18.366 --> 00:01:19.866
is needed for construction.

00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:21.566
Cement has been used for millennia,

00:01:21.566 --> 00:01:25.033
to build structures like the
Pantheon and Roman aqueducts,

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.100
to highways and parking garages.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.300
Lots of parking garages.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.033
Globally, the production of cement

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.600
accounts of 7% of yearly CO2 emissions.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.600
And that's largely because
of how cement is created.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.633
The main ingredient to cement
is a substance called clinker.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.733
In order to produce this,

00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:44.133
limestone is heated to high temperatures.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.733
And usually, this heat is generated

00:01:45.733 --> 00:01:48.333
by fossil fuels, releasing CO2.

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:50.699
Meanwhile, the chemical
reactions inside the kiln

00:01:50.699 --> 00:01:53.766
release even more CO2 in the process.

00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:56.633
Companies are working to reduce
the amount of clinker used.

00:01:56.633 --> 00:01:59.466
Others are testing
substitutes, including fly ash,

00:01:59.466 --> 00:02:01.100
which is the residue left in chimneys

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.433
of coal-burning furnaces, or
slag from iron production.

00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:06.400
But the drawbacks are serious.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.366
These new techniques come with a price tag

00:02:08.366 --> 00:02:11.333
sometimes triple the cost
of the traditional process.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:12.966
And since cement is holding many

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.633
of the world's structures together,

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:18.266
alternative recipes make
contractors and regulators uneasy.

00:02:20.466 --> 00:02:22.800
Steel is just as important as cement,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.733
and as cities grow, global demand

00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:29.266
is expected to rise by
50% between 2019 and 2050.

00:02:29.266 --> 00:02:31.666
But its process involves
purifying iron ore

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:35.333
in blast furnaces, with a
refined form of coal called coke.

00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:39.000
And just like cement, this
production produces a lot of CO2.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.633
In Europe, blast furnace owners

00:02:40.633 --> 00:02:42.866
are testing hydrogen as an alternative way

00:02:42.866 --> 00:02:44.899
to take the carbon out of iron ore.

00:02:44.899 --> 00:02:48.266
But again, so far, it's way
too expensive to go mainstream.

00:02:48.266 --> 00:02:50.466
About double the cost of using coke.

00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:51.933
There's one thing you can do with steel

00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:53.533
that you can't do with cement.

00:02:53.533 --> 00:02:55.300
And that is recycle.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.800
Instead of producing more
steel in the first place,

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.666
we can use what we already have.

00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:03.066
Increasing the use of steel
recycling is now commonly seen

00:03:03.066 --> 00:03:05.466
as critical to reducing carbon emissions.

00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:09.500
Now agriculture requires
a multi-pronged effort,

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.166
as it is responsible for nearly 25%

00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:14.200
of global CO2 emissions.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.966
The practice of controlled
burns after harvests,

00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:18.800
the use of inorganic fertilizers

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.400
that release methane and
nitrous oxide into the air,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.500
the destruction of
rainforests for ranching,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.566
and even livestock flatulence,
all need to be addressed

00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:29.800
to put a dent in
agriculture's carbon output.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.033
Some hope can be seen in the US,

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:35.600
as demands for beef products
have dropped significantly.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.500
Additionally, interest in alternatives,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.533
like Beyond Meat and Impossible Burgers,

00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:41.533
have soared in recent years.

00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:43.666
And for those who can't quit beef,

00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:46.233
scientists are developing
climate-proof cows,

00:03:46.233 --> 00:03:49.566
with digestive systems
that produce less methane.

00:03:49.566 --> 00:03:51.833
But implementing these solutions globally

00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:53.466
remains an uphill battle.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.366
Even as more people in Europe and the US

00:03:55.366 --> 00:03:57.266
take up vegetarian alternatives,

00:03:57.266 --> 00:04:00.333
increased meat demand in China
and other developing nations

00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:02.533
means that globally,
animal product consumption

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:05.300
is expected to rise 60% by 2050.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.899
You are the last best hope of Earth.

00:04:08.899 --> 00:04:12.266
We are in the beginning
of a mass extinction,

00:04:12.266 --> 00:04:15.033
and all you can talk about is money

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:18.733
and fairy tales of
eternal economic growth.

00:04:18.733 --> 00:04:19.766
How dare you.

00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:23.466
It'll take policy makers and companies

00:04:23.466 --> 00:04:26.066
years of diligent work and collaboration

00:04:26.066 --> 00:04:29.466
to move industry away from
its most polluting methods.

00:04:29.466 --> 00:04:32.200
But each of these industries
is working on answers,

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.866
with some executives confident

00:04:33.866 --> 00:04:36.366
they can be both green and show a profit.

